;; CLean — E2-PILOT: single-problem memory-ablation apparatus shakedown.
;;
;; REGISTRATION #2 through this pipeline, and the first from the V3 memory
;; programme (futon3c). The predecessor design is the eleven-times-reviewed
;; DarkTower/MemoryAblationPreregistration.lean (mathlib4), whose ValidatedTrace
;; refactor (2026-08-01, codex-1) makes an unvalidated trace untypeable into a
;; verdict. This file is the EXECUTABLE registration of its PILOT stage.
;;
;; PILOT DISCIPLINE (the process rule, stated first): this is an apparatus
;; shakedown plus first identity-rate measurements on ONE problem-pair. n=1.
;; It validates the isolation boundary, the trace canonicalization, and the
;; receipt sensors. It CANNOT validate the load-bearing rubric and will not
;; claim to; every effect-shaped endpoint below is :role :secondary and
;; labelled hypothesis-generating. The confirmation panel is manufactured by
;; the V3 cohort's control arm (fresh preregistered window — the corpus
;; archaeology found exactly ONE strong pair in 50 candidates, see
;; panel-nomination-sweep-20260801.md) and registers separately.
;;
;; THE GENERALIZED INERTNESS PRECONDITION (from the ants 10x10-grid failure,
;; claude-4 2026-08-01): before measuring whether mechanism M helps, establish
;; that the task cannot be solved without M — and ENUMERATE the paths ruled
;; out. For withholding a memory, four paths could make the contrast inert:
;;   (1) in-tree content   — the problem tree carries the operative plan;
;;   (2) library search    — reachable by grep in pinned Mathlib;
;;   (3) model competence  — the runner closes it without any external content;
;;   (4) corpus emptiness  — nothing would have been delivered anyway.
;; The LB axis justification below carries the per-path evidence for this
;; pair. Path (4) inverts for ablation designs: the manipulation check is
;; that the withheld memory WOULD have been delivered (it is offered on
;; every control run) and IS absent from ablated runs' offered sets.

