   {:id :lb-identity-vs-floor :direction :informational :role :secondary
    :sensor {:field :trace/decision-sequence-hash :source "as :identity-floor"
             :coverage-precondition "as :identity-floor"
             :coverage-check {:status :met-by-construction :check "same gate"}}
    :note "NON-CONFIRMATORY: n=1 problem. A LB-ablated sequence identical to control on k/n runs is per-pair evidence AGAINST the pair's load-bearing designation — recorded, not promoted"}
   {:id :inc-identity-vs-floor :direction :informational :role :secondary
    :sensor {:field :trace/decision-sequence-hash :source "as :identity-floor"
             :coverage-precondition "as :identity-floor"
             :coverage-check {:status :met-by-construction :check "same gate"}}
    :note "the predicted null, read as an identity rate against the floor — direct evidence, no power argument"}]

  ;; Operational stop rules, now expressible via the generalised predicate ABI
  ;; (bend #3 fix, d8a8f7b): each names an executable :predicate over a real
  ;; ExperimentTrace field, so Lean emits a genuine `fires`, not prose. Fields
  ;; match codex-2's measured-variation fixture (:boundary-refused, :completed-runs).
  :stop-rules
  [{:id :boundary-refusal
    :predicate {:kind :bool-field :field :boundary-refused}
    :fires-when "any run's wrapper exits 78 (probe failure) after e3 has discharged"
    :action :abandon-run
    :note "a refusal after the gate means the boundary regressed mid-pilot; the pilot's product is apparatus knowledge, so this outcome is a finding, not noise"}
   {:id :budget-cap
    :predicate {:kind :nat-ge :field :completed-runs :threshold 15}
    :fires-when "the 16th run would start (cap-cell-runs 15 vs estimated 12)"
    :action :abandon-run}]

  :dispositions []   ;; every unit runs once to completion; no outcome changes
                     ;; what a unit is. Empty rather than omitted — the absence
                     ;; is a statement. (The cohort's re-queue disposition, with
                     ;; both integrity fields, lives in ITS registration.)

  ;; Total: every trace the pilot can emit maps to a named outcome.
  :decision
  {:boundary-failed        :apparatus-defect-isolation
   :instrument-gate-failed :apparatus-defect-trace-sensor
   :delivery-failed        :apparatus-defect-ablation-mechanism
   :incomplete             :pilot-incomplete-not-interpretable
   :complete               :apparatus-validated-report-identity-rates
   :mixed                  :apparatus-partially-validated-enumerate-defects}

  :assumptions
  [{:id :filter-equals-ship :kind :assumption
    :holds "filter-at-dispatch (mechanism b) is equivalent to shipping a store without the withheld memory (mechanism a): the runner's view differs only by the withheld entry"
    :holds-while "the memory graph is a star forest — no memory reaches the surfaced set through a shared pattern with another memory"
    :breaks-when "multi-attachment populates the graph: removing M then changes what ELSE surfaces through shared patterns, and (a) and (b) diverge"
    :evidence "V2 sect 4.6: multi-attachment was always representable and never written. The d-separation form (outcome ⊥ withheld-content | surfaced set) is now RECEIPT-CONFIRMED: M-diagramprover's Q3 receipt (landed 2026-08-02, futon3c 2e50339d + 504be25c, engine-verified and independently cross-checked) proves filter-at-dispatch is a FAITHFUL do(withhold M) on the current star_forest topology, and confirms this assumption's :breaks-when directly — under populated_graph the path [:M-in-store → :shared-patterns → :V12-minus-M] opens and mechanism (a) and (b) diverge. Oracle cross-validation (dagitty/bnlearn/networkx/y0) in flight; a verdict change would bell a correction"
    :on-break :invalidates-ablation-mechanism-equivalence
    :discharge-condition "runtime assertion BEFORE EVERY DISPATCH: store query asserting no memory carries >1 reviewed pattern attachment; fails loudly (refusal, not log line)"}
   {:id :recall-regime-stable :kind :assumption
    :holds "the recall architecture is constant across the pilot window (:recall-system :v1.2-receipt-instrumented on every receipt)"
    :holds-while "no arm commissioning, decommissioning, or recall-system version change during the window"
    :breaks-when "any receipt in the window carries a different version tag"
    :evidence "the E1 back-fill's regime discovery (boundary at 50916c84): the pooled 60.95% was deployment history, not competition — a dated assumption about the measurement regime is exactly what nearly got headlined"
    :on-break :invalidates-cross-run-pooling
    :discharge-condition "per-run check of the receipt's version tag; any mismatch marks the run :regime-tainted and excludes it from pooling"
    ;; RESIDUAL (R-0 re-read, claude-4 2026-08-02 -- a declared assumption does
    ;; not protect you if the :breaks-when names the wrong failure mode): the
    ;; version-tag check is a RUNTIME guard (the strong form) and catches any
    ;; regime change that BUMPS the version -- broader than the commissioning
    ;; enumeration in :holds-while. But it does NOT catch a SILENT regime change
